<HelpTab>
    <FluentText>
        A projection program is a sequence of screens shown on a kiosk's projector or display, such as a welcome
        message, a video, the scoreboard or a dashboard. Build them on
        <a href="/manage/projectionprograms">Projection</a>.
    </FluentText>

    <HelpSection Title="Building a program">
        <ol>
            <li>Select <strong>New</strong>, and give the program a <strong>Program Name</strong> and optional description.</li>
            <li>Select the program in the list on the left.</li>
            <li>Drag steps from the toolbox on the right into the flow in the middle, after <strong>START</strong>.
                The built-in steps are <strong>Show Text</strong>, <strong>Play a Video</strong>, <strong>Dashboard</strong>,
                <strong>Live Capture</strong> (a camera or capture device) and <strong>Delay</strong>, which keeps the
                previous screen up.</li>
            <li>Fill in each step's settings, such as the text, the video file (pick one from the File Manager or
                upload it), or the dashboard.</li>
            <li>Right-click a step for more options, such as deleting it, then save.</li>
        </ol>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Live venue data in text">
        <FluentText>
            Text steps can show live data instead of fixed words. Change <strong>Text source</strong> from
            <strong>Fixed text</strong> to Last game winner, Today's top score or Opening hours today. The screen
            keeps it up to date while it's showing. Set <strong>Fallback text</strong> for when there's no data yet or
            the kiosk is offline.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Starting a program on a kiosk">
        <FluentText>Programs are started by:</FluentText>
        <ul>
            <li>an <a href="/help/automation">automation rule</a>, for example when a game ends;</li>
            <li>a dashboard <strong>Button</strong> widget set to Trigger Projection Program.</li>
        </ul>
    </HelpSection>
</HelpTab>
